(:include "tiers/melee.domain")
(:include "tiers/feed.domain")
(:include "tiers/idle.domain")

// Grazer: fight back when something hostile is near, else eat or drink, else idle. Three tiers in priority order.
//
// Teaches: priority by branch order between shared tiers (fight > feed > idle), each root branch guarded by the
// tier's precondition axiom (see mouse.domain for why our roots need guards where the source has none).
// Source: Space Station 14 (MIT), `RuminantHostileCompound` in Resources/Prototypes/NPCs/mob.yml at commit
// 614f030530578e248a2393dd71ee9813d68d800d:
// https://github.com/space-wizards/space-station-14/blob/614f030530578e248a2393dd71ee9813d68d800d/Resources/Prototypes/NPCs/mob.yml
// Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2017-2026 Space Wizards Federation; see src/examples/canon/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
// Adapted (YAML prototypes re-written in our domain language).
// Deviations: guards on the root branches. Who counts as hostile (in SS14 a faction rule: a grazer turns on whoever
// attacked it) is the host sensor's decision; the domain only reads `(hostile ?target)`.
// Not ported: `RuminantCompound`, the peaceful variant (feed > idle, the mouse's shape).
//
// Facts and primitives: see tiers/melee.domain, tiers/feed.domain and tiers/idle.domain.

(:domain Grazer top_level_domain

    (:method (behave) top_level_method

        (fight
            (and
                (#melee_target ?target)
            )
            (
                (melee ?target)
            )
        )

        (eat
            (and
                (#feed_target ?item)
            )
            (
                (feed ?item)
            )
        )

        (idle
            ()
            (
                (idle)
            )
        )
    )
)
